      "id": "a2.grammar.practice-countable-dinner",
      "level": "A2",
      "topics": ["grammar"],
      "title": "Dinner for friends",
      "text": "Tonight Nora is making dinner for a few friends. She doesn't have much time, so she writes a quick list. She has a little rice and some cheese, but she needs a few tomatoes and some bread. There isn't much milk in the fridge, and there aren't many eggs. She also wants some fruit for dessert. At the store she spends a lot of money, but the dinner is a big success.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "original"
      }
    }
